## Notes

- The preimage-keyed memo costs re-walking a repeated subtree's structure on hits (the preimage needs child hashes to exist); each node's sha256 and record write are still skipped, and the memo remains an optimisation whose absence changes nothing — per the ruling's "optimisation only" requirement.
- Deferred as instructed: unreachable-record diagnostics and scalar-type revalidation on read (the hash check covers typing; revisits at D4/D5); the UTF-16 length-prefix note stays D3's byte-rules scope.
